{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_source_guides_all_in_one_for_researchers_guide", "label": "All-in-one for Researchers guide", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Onboarding guide for researchers to launch a first small-transformer experiment (locally via torchrun or on Beaker), customize training-loop components, scale to larger models at high MFU, and troubleshoot common issues."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_all_in_one_for_researchers_fork_workflow", "label": "Fork-and-install workflow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "For rapid experimentation researchers should fork OLMo-core per project and install it editable (pip install -e '.[all]') rather than depend on it as a package, so architecture/data recipes can be edited directly; Python >=3.10 and PyTorch installed first."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_all_in_one_for_researchers_config_dataclass_pattern", "label": "Config dataclass pattern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wrapping experiment hyperparameters in a Config-derived dataclass is optional but (1) tracks all hyperparameters and serializes to JSON (uploadable to W&B or saved with the checkpoint), and (2) yields a free CLI parser mapping args (even nested, via dot-notation) to config fields through Config.merge()."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_all_in_one_for_researchers_dry_run_mode", "label": "Dry-run mode", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The --dry-run flag validates that config overrides resolve correctly before spending GPU time on a real launch."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_all_in_one_for_researchers_beaker_launch", "label": "Beaker launch workflow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "OLMo-core ships a lightweight gantry-like launch CLI (python -m olmo_core.launch.beaker) plus prebuilt Beaker images with all dependencies (OLMoCoreBeakerImage), so runs launch on Beaker without building an image; --shared-filesystem signals ranks share a filesystem (e.g. weka), and reading data from a weka mount is much faster than streaming over HTTP."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_all_in_one_for_researchers_trainmodule_abstraction", "label": "TrainModule abstraction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A TrainModule abstracts the model, optimizer and checkpointing away from the Trainer so the general-purpose Trainer can adapt to nearly any deep-learning task; TransformerTrainModule works out-of-the-box for text transformers, while BasicTrainModule is the recommended starting point for writing your own."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_all_in_one_for_researchers_callback_system", "label": "Trainer callback system", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The training loop is customized via a rich callback API (subclasses of Callback added by name or Trainer.add_callback()); ConsoleLogger, SpeedMonitor, GarbageCollector and Checkpointer callbacks are considered mandatory and auto-added unless the user provides them."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_all_in_one_for_researchers_scaling_strategy", "label": "Transformer scaling strategy", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scaling guidelines for TransformerTrainModule: use FSDP (or HSDP depending on model size, node count, bandwidth) instead of DDP at >=1B params; do NOT use TP/CP/activation-checkpointing unless you OOM at a single-instance micro-batch, and always use the largest micro-batch that fits; when a single-instance micro-batch won't fit, first try minimal 'budget'-mode activation checkpointing and raise the budget to the highest that fits; always enable torch.compile (faster and lower peak CUDA memory). Supports DP/TP/CP/EP and experimental PP (TransformerPipelineTrainModule); dense models up to ~70B are trainable at reasonable MFU without pipelining."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_all_in_one_for_researchers_finetuning_workflow", "label": "Fine-tuning workflow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same Trainer supports fine-tuning as well as pretraining: convert pretrained (e.g. HuggingFace) weights into the format the Trainer expects, then set --load-path so the Trainer loads them at the start of the run."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_all_in_one_for_researchers_troubleshooting", "label": "Training troubleshooting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Asynchronous CUDA kernel execution makes Python-level traces misleading; set CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1 (or launch --debug) for accurate stack traces. On OOM reduce rank_microbatch_size, then add activation checkpointing. Diagnose throughput by first checking batch-load time (logged by SpeedMonitorCallback), then capture traces with ProfilerCallback (view in Perfetto UI). Reproduce distributed-only bugs with run_distributed_test."}, {"id": "docs_source_guides_all_in_one_for_researchers_scaling_book", "label": "Scaling Book", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": "https://jax-ml.github.io/scaling-book", "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_config_config", "label": "olmo_core.config.Config", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_launch_beaker", "label": "olmo_core.launch.beaker", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_launch_beaker_olmocorebeakerimage", "label": "olmo_core.launch.beaker.OLMoCoreBeakerImage", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_train_trainer", "label": "olmo_core.train.Trainer", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "src_olmo_core_train_duration", "label": "olmo_core.train.Duration", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/source/guides/all_in_one_for_researchers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": n